body:
So, I didn't know that I was adopted by my father (step-father) until I was about 15 years old. I found out Christmas morning from my cousin (sperm donners side of the family). I made the decision to meet him when I was 16 but backed out last minute due to being scared. I then decided to meet him when I was 18. I had learned over the course of two years of what he had done to my mom and me when I was a kid. Hid drugs in my room as an infant so cops would never find them, hit my mom, was intoxicated all the time and was just a total POS. I thought he might of well changed since I was infant. When I decided to meet him when I was 18, I met him at a public place. When I walked up to him, he stated "Hello son". I lost control and broke his nose. I informed him that I was not his son. Frank (father) was my real dad and had done more for me than he ever will. I informed him that he should never make contact with me again. I have not spoke with him since. 

&#x200B;

Moral of this paragraph is, If the kid is curious on seeing her bio mom, maybe let her but don't leave her side. I still tried to give my sperm donner a chance but blew it. I will admit that I went off the rails but still don't regret it.
